  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe allocation of voting power for each pool is determined by the user’s input weight array.\nHowever, if a pool is inactive, the loop skips it during processing. This can cause the actual allocation to differ significantly from the user’s expectations.\n\nFor example, suppose there are three pools: `pool1`, `pool2`, and `pool3`.\nThe owner intends to assign weights of `[10, 30, 60]`, corresponding to 10%, 30%, and 60% of the total voting power.\n\nIf `pool2`’s gauge is killed before the owner invokes `vote`, the system recalculates the weights as `[10, 60]`.\nThis changes the proportions to `10/70 ≈ 15%` and `60/70 ≈ 85%`, which deviates significantly from the owner’s intended distribution.\n\nMoreover, the total base of the weights is not validated.\nIf the user provides a very small total weight base, the resulting allocation error can become significantly larger.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n1.check total weights\n2.ensure gauge is all active",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/GaugeV2.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/RewardHYBR.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console2.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\n\ncontract ERC20Mock is ERC20 {\n    constructor() ERC20(\"ERC20Mock\", \"E20M\") {}\n    function mint(address account, uint256 amount) external {\n        _mint(account, amount);\n    }\n    function burn(address account, uint256 amount) external {\n        _burn(account, amount);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract C4PoC is C4PoCTestbed {\n\n    address public gaugeV2;\n\n    address alice = address(0x1);\n    address bob = address(0x2);\n    address carol = address(0x3);\n    address eve = address(0x4);\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n    }\n\n    //POC5. Vote weight changed after gauge killed.\n    //1,percent changed , 2.weight changed.\n    function test_POC5() public {\n        vm.startPrank(address(minter));\n        hybr.mint(alice, 100e18);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), type(uint256).max);\n        gHybr.deposit(10e18, alice);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        gHybr.setVoter(address(voter));\n\n        bribeFactoryV3.initialize(address(voter), address(gaugeManager), address(permissionsRegistry), address(tokenHandler));\n\n        ERC20Mock token1 = new ERC20Mock();\n        ERC20Mock token2 = new ERC20Mock();\n        ERC20Mock token3 = new ERC20Mock();\n\n        permissionsRegistry.setRoleFor(address(this), \"GOVERNANCE\");\n\n        tokenHandler.whitelistToken(address(token1));\n        tokenHandler.whitelistToken(address(token2));\n        tokenHandler.whitelistToken(address(token3));\n        tokenHandler.whitelistConnector(address(token1));\n        tokenHandler.whitelistConnector(address(token2));\n        tokenHandler.whitelistConnector(address(token3));\n\n        address pool1 = thenaFiFactory.createPair(address(token1), address(token2), false);\n        address pool2 = thenaFiFactory.createPair(address(token2), address(token3), false);\n        address pool3 = thenaFiFactory.createPair(address(token1), address(token3), false);\n\n        (address g1,,)  = gaugeManager.createGauge(pool1,0);\n        (address g2,,)  = gaugeManager.createGauge(pool2,0);\n        (address g3,,)  = gaugeManager.createGauge(pool3,0);\n\n        address[] memory pools = new address[](3);\n        pools[0] = address(pool1);\n        pools[1] = address(pool2);\n        pools[2] = address(pool3);\n\n        uint256[] memory weights = new uint256[](3);\n        weights[0] = 10;\n        weights[1] = 30;\n        weights[2] = 60;\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 weeks + 301);\n\n        uint256 snapshotId = vm.snapshot();\n\n        //killed g2 and vote.\n        gaugeManager.killGauge(g2);\n        gHybr.vote(pools, weights);\n\n        uint256 weight = voter.weights(address(pool1));\n        console2.log(\"1:\", weight);\n\n        vm.revertTo(snapshotId);\n\n        //not killed g2 and vote.\n        gHybr.vote(pools, weights);\n\n        weight = voter.weights(address(pool1));\n        console2.log(\"2:\", weight);\n    }\n\n```\n\n```shell\n  1: 1414865958171970623\n  2: 990406170720379436\n```",
